From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:11:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/PlatformBootManagerLib: Apply capsules on
 disk, keep the flash safe

With DRIVERS_EFI_CAPSULE_ON_DISK_SUPPORT, coreboot sees the capsules on
disk announced in OsIndications and lets the SMMSTORE handler write the
whole flash until the next boot, but the payload only applies capsules
that come as HOBs and boots on: the capsules on disk are never applied,
the bit in OsIndications stays set, and every boot hands the writable
flash over to Driver#### options, option ROMs and the OS, past a BIOS
lock. Capsules in memory have the same issue on a smaller scale, the
reset coming only after the console, Driver#### options included.

Handle the capsules of the boot before EndOfDxe, where FmpDxe still
accepts SetImage(), in PlatformProcessCapsules():
- clear the bit in OsIndications first, so that the next boot is a
  normal one whatever happens;
- with a battery, wait up to a minute for it to be charging or above
  25% before writing, postponing the update otherwise;
- process the HOB capsules as before, then connect the devices and load
  the files of \EFI\UpdateCapsule on the EFI system partitions (the
  payload has no PEI to load them on a later boot as CapsuleOnDisk.c
  expects), delete them and process them with ProcessCapsuleImage(),
  showing the result recorded in Capsule####;
- reset after applying a capsule, before the console is connected;
- otherwise give up the whole flash access with
  SmmStoreLibEndAnyBlockAccess() and boot on, or reset if that fails.

Whether the flash is writable is asked to the SMMSTORE handler, with a
one byte read of the whole flash, not inferred from the variables:
coreboot and the variable driver can read OsIndications differently from
a store with an interrupted or crafted update of it.

Capsules that need a second pass after EndOfDxe, for device firmware
with embedded drivers, are no longer processed: the only FMP instance is
the system firmware, locked by FmpDxe at EndOfDxe anyway.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 .../PlatformBootManager.c                     |  45 +-
 .../PlatformBootManager.h                     |  13 +
 .../PlatformBootManagerLib.inf                |   7 +
 .../PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformCapsule.c  | 538 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 561 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformCapsule.c

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
index b235733a47..5fa9462bb6 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
@@ -373,7 +373,6 @@ PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole (
   VOID
   )
 {
-  EFI_STATUS                    Status;
   EFI_INPUT_KEY                 Enter;
   EFI_INPUT_KEY                 CustomKey;
   EFI_INPUT_KEY                 Down;
@@ -413,21 +412,10 @@ PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole (
   EfiBootManagerAddKeyOptionVariable (NULL, (UINT16)BootOption.OptionNumber, 0, &Down, NULL);
 
   //
-  // Process update capsules that don't contain embedded drivers.
+  // Apply the update capsules of this boot, if any: the whole flash must not
+  // stay writable for option ROMs, Driver#### options or an OS.
   //
-  ConsoleInitialized = FALSE;
-  if (GetBootModeHob () == BOOT_ON_FLASH_UPDATE) {
-    // TODO: when enabling capsule support for laptops, add a battery check here
-    PlatformConsoleInit ();
-    ConsoleInitialized = TRUE;
-
-    BootSplashApply ();
-
-    Status = ProcessCapsules ();
-    if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-      DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "%a(): ProcessCapsule() failed with: %r\n", __func__, Status));
-    }
-  }
+  ConsoleInitialized = PlatformProcessCapsules ();
 
   //
   // Register a callback to show a message when the Boot Manager Menu hotkey is pressed.
@@ -487,33 +475,6 @@ PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole (
     EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption ();
   }
 
-  //
-  // Active BOOT_ON_FLASH_UPDATE mode means that at least one capsule has been
-  // discovered by a bootloader and passed for further processing into EDK which
-  // created EFI_HOB_TYPE_UEFI_CAPSULE HOB(s).
-  //
-  // Process update capsules that weren't processed on the first call to
-  // ProcessCapsules() in PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole().
-  //
-  if (GetBootModeHob () == BOOT_ON_FLASH_UPDATE) {
-    // TODO: when enabling capsule support for laptops, add a battery check here
-    Status = ProcessCapsules ();
-    if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-      DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "%a(): ProcessCapsule() failed with: %r\n", __func__, Status));
-    }
-
-    //
-    // Reset the system to disable SMI handler in order to exclude the
-    // possibility of it being used outside of the firmware.
-    //
-    // In practice, this will rarely execute because even the first
-    // ProcessCapsules() invocation might do a reset if all capsules were
-    // processed and at least one of them needed a reset.  This is just to catch
-    // a case when this doesn't happen which is possible on error.
-    //
-    gRT->ResetSystem (EfiResetCold, EFI_SUCCESS, 0, NULL);
-  }
-
   //
   // Process TPM PPI request
   //
